    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d667">

                <pb facs="0960" n="950" xml:id="pg950"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Potsdam/8–745</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Truman to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-23">July 23, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Number 310. Please deliver the following message to Generalissimo Chiang
                    Kai-shek: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I refer to your message of 19 July quoting your telegram to
                            Generalissimo Stalin.</p>
                        <p>I asked that you carry out the Yalta agreement but I had not asked that
                            you make any concession in excess of that agreement. If you and
                            Generalissimo Stalin differ as to the correct interpretation of the
                            Yalta agreement, I hope you will arrange for Soong to return to Moscow
                            and continue your efforts to reach complete understanding. Truman.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Truman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
